title: Your server did draw the old title under 'health \ jbb'. Whether your buffer still showed it when you looked, your logs cannot tell.
pid: 87ab808d-3a20-44a5-ada3-cc75ea208114
body: |2-
  Tracy copied your data as it stood at 20:34 UTC on 2026-11-13, when you opened the
  diff view, and opened the diff view on the copy. It gives the headlines the same numbers as in
  your example (the 'vnid 4l' of 'health \ jbb'), and draws the old title, 'medical, recent <2026-11-04 Wed> mess',
  directly under 'health \ jbb'. Replaying what you did between 20:34 and 20:38
  never removed it. But your server's logs record only which requests Emacs sent,
  not what the buffer held, so they cannot show whether the old title was still
  there when you looked, or folded out of sight. A folded headline looks like a
  leaf except for the '...' at its end.
  From now on, the server keeps each open view's last rendered text and last saved
  buffer in the folder 'views' of its run folder (beside 'server-to-user.log'),
  so the next case can be read. Those files hold your views' text, private
  skgrepos included.
contains:
- ef56e0e2-3992-4121-85cd-562be0894b9a
- 0d448661-64dd-44c4-a38e-09bfcc9b7196
- 8a89562e-ba36-4cd9-8080-e9d8f16d3b42
